  "narrative": "Select H30–H41 for the current 12-claim analysis batch. These tests localize the accepted global feature_010 association: H30–H35 estimate the feature_010=1 versus feature_010=0 mean difference in the upper and lower quartiles of each research signature, H36–H38 estimate it in the positive stratum of each assigned binary marker, and H39–H40 estimate it in long versus short log-persistence quartiles. H41 tests feature_041 within the feature_010=1 stratum to assess whether a secondary binary assay remains associated in the dominant stratum. I avoided exact continuous exposure comparisons and chose subgroup threshold comparisons with sufficient expected cell sizes. This batch prioritizes biological and clinical stratification of the strongest observed association before pursuing additional interactions or broad binary predictors.",
  "research_notes": "Analyze batch selected: H30-H41. Scientific goal: characterize feature_010 heterogeneity across research-signature quartiles, assigned-marker positive strata, and clinical log-persistence quartiles, plus residual feature_041 effect within feature_010=1. Avoid invalid exact-continuous claims H1-H3, H10, H12 unless re-expressed as threshold/binarized contrasts. H13 remains accepted active. Future analyze should include feature_010-by-marker/signature interactions (H14-H18, H25-H29) if heterogeneity is important, and broad binary predictors H19-H24/H42-H44 for additional discoveries. Validate H13 in appraise after assessing new evidence if still appropriate."
